fss-adsb (1.0.1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * debian: ship a templated systemd unit, fss-adsb@.service. The instance
    name selects an environment file /etc/fss-adsb/<instance>.conf, matching
    the one-instance-per-FSS-server deployment model; instances are not
    enabled by default. An example configuration is installed under
    /usr/share/doc/fss-adsb/examples/.
  * main: add --help/-h and --version.

 -- Scott Parlane <sjp@canterburyairpatrol.org>  Fri, 10 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000

fss-adsb (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * dump1090: close the socket when the receive thread observes a dropped
    connection, fixing a file-descriptor leak per drop/reconnect cycle.
  * dump1090: take the ADS-B callback as a constructor parameter so it is in
    place before the receive thread starts (closes a registration race).
  * dump1090: guard empty groundspeed/track/vertrate (MSG,4) and squawk
    (MSG,6) fields so a missing field is not reported as a valid zero value;
    clamp ground speed and squawk parsing like the other numeric fields.
  * dump1090: handle MSG,2 (surface position) explicitly; it reports nothing
    but keeps the aircraft's last_seen fresh.
  * dump1090: cap the reconnect backoff exactly at 30s; pass getaddrinfo()
    hints (SOCK_STREAM, AI_ADDRCONFIG) when resolving the dump1090 host.
  * main: send the position report outside the aircraft-map lock so a stalled
    TLS send cannot block stale-aircraft eviction.
  * fss-reporter: drop client_lock; rely on flight-safety-system's internally
    synchronised connection pointer so a blocking reconnect no longer stalls
    reportAircraft() on the dump1090 receive thread.
  * Bump version to 1.0.0; drop unused libtool/pkg-config-install/
    pthread-check machinery and undefined Makefile.am variables.
  * README: the example now points at dump1090's SBS-1 port 30003 (not the
    raw AVR port 30002, which fss-adsb cannot parse).
  * debian: modernise packaging style
    - Switch from debian/compat to debhelper-compat (= 13) in Build-Depends
    - Update Standards-Version to 4.7.0
    - Add ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends} to binary package Depends
    - Fix debian/copyright placeholders
    - Drop bogus dh_auto_configure override
  * debian: Section utils; drop unused systemd and autotools-dev
    Build-Depends; depend on every FSS library actually linked (libfss,
    libfss-transport, libfss-transport-ssl, libfss-client-ssl), all
    versioned >= 1.0.2.
  * ci: valgrind now runs with --track-fds=yes to catch fd leaks.

 -- Scott Parlane <sjp@canterburyairpatrol.org>  Fri, 12 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000

